family: net-snmp
what: trap
transport: v3
address: 2001:db8::10
verification: tested
verification_detail: CI starts real snmpd with these lines (its coldStart trap) and runs the snmptrap test as written, v2c and v3 (SHA-256 where the tools have it, and SHA-1 with another user name), and v2c over IPv6.
reference: net-snmp manual pages: snmpd.conf(5) (trap2sink, trapsess, createUser), snmp.conf(5) (defCommunity, defSecurityName, defAuthType…), snmptrap(1)
does: Makes snmpd send its traps to Woodshed (SNMPv3), and gives a test trap to send with snmptrap.
check: Search Events for type Traps: the trap snmpd sends at start (coldStart) and the test trap each appear once; `woodshed snmp status` counts them.
placeholders: <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Add the same user in Woodshed first: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, name monitor, SHA-1 and AES-128, with the same passphrases (at least 8 characters each).
- snmpd sends v3 traps as its own engine, with a user of that engine: the createUser line makes it (snmpd 5.7 and later don't make one from the trapsess line's passphrases, and log "USM unknown security name"). The user gets no access to the agent's data unless an rouser or rwuser line grants it. If the poll snippet adds the same user, keep one createUser line.
- Keep snmpd.conf readable by root only, and ~/.snmp/snmp.conf by you only (chmod 600 ~/.snmp/snmp.conf): they hold the passphrases.
- The test trap's OID is under the documentation enterprise number (32473), so it can't be mistaken for a real alarm.
---- part file "/etc/snmp/snmpd.conf": Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd); it sends a trap when it starts
# Woodshed: send traps (SNMPv3).
createUser monitor SHA <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> AES <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
trapsess -v 3 -u monitor -l authPriv udp6:[2001:db8::10]:162
---- part file "~/.snmp/snmp.conf": For the test trap: snmptrap reads its user and passphrases from this file, not the command line
defSecurityName monitor
defSecurityLevel authPriv
defAuthType SHA
defAuthPassphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
defPrivType AES
defPrivPassphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
---- part command "": Send a test trap
snmptrap -v 3 udp6:[2001:db8::10]:162 '' 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.0.1 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.1.1.0 s "Test trap for Woodshed from $(hostname)"
==== text
# /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf: Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd); it sends a trap when it starts
# Woodshed: send traps (SNMPv3).
createUser monitor SHA <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> AES <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
trapsess -v 3 -u monitor -l authPriv udp6:[2001:db8::10]:162

# ~/.snmp/snmp.conf: For the test trap: snmptrap reads its user and passphrases from this file, not the command line
defSecurityName monitor
defSecurityLevel authPriv
defAuthType SHA
defAuthPassphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
defPrivType AES
defPrivPassphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>

# Send a test trap
snmptrap -v 3 udp6:[2001:db8::10]:162 '' 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.0.1 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.1.1.0 s "Test trap for Woodshed from $(hostname)"
